<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n6943" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Cassander</span></b> , dri, m., =
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Κάσσανδρος</span>. <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<i>A son of Antipater</i>, <i>and king of
				Macedonia after the death of Alexander the Great</i>, <i><span class="en">Just. 15,
				1 sq.</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Curt. 10, 10, 9</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Cic. Off.
				2, 14, 48</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Nep. Eum. 13, 3</span></i>.—After
			him was named the town Cassandrea, <i><span class="en">Liv. 44,
				11, 2</span></i>. —</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<i>A Greek astrologer</i>, <i><span class="en">Cic. Div.
				2, 42, 88</span></i>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
